{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Overview}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Overview}
\pard\keepn \b\fs28\cf1 Overview
\par \pard \plain\fs24 The trackerball option provides an alternative method of adjustment of some parameters to provide a 'two handed' operation of the SEM
\par 
\par The trackerball comprises a ball which may be moved in two dimensions to control one or two parameters. The parameter adjustment is non linear, spinning the ball results in accelerated adjustment.
\par 
\par The trackerball also has three buttons, pressing each button selects predefined parameters for adjustment.
\par 
\par The current parameters being controlled are displayed in the \uldb \b Trackerball Toolbar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Trackerball_Toolbar}\plain\fs24  
\par \pard 
\par 
\par See also \uldb Installation\plain\fs24 {\v Installation}
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Installation}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Installation}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} General Properties}
\b\fs28\cf1 Installation
\par \pard \plain\fs24 On installation of the trackerball it is essential to define the Serial Port to be used for the trackerball, this is done in the Administrator - configuration form.
\par 
\par The Trackerball toolbar is displayed by selecting \b View\plain\fs24  - \b Toolbars\plain\fs24  and checking the \b TKB\plain\fs24  checkbox.
\par 
\par Unless the Port is defined, is successfully configured, and the Trackerball licence is present the TKB checkbox will not appear or will not be enabled.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Trackerball Toolbar}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Trackerball_Toolbar}
\pard\keepn \b\fs28\cf1 Trackerball Toolbar
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx5905\cellx9005\pard\intbl The Trackerball toolbar displays the parameters currently being controlled by the Trackerball.
\par\intbl To display the toolbar see \uldb installation\plain\fs24 {\v Installation}
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl To change the parameters assigned to each button double click on the parameter in the toolbar to display the \uldb Selection Dialog\plain\fs24 {\v Selection_Dialog}\cell\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
\par \page
